  "causality-over-sequence": {
   "statement": "Between any two adjacent beats of a factual narrative you must be able to say \"but\" or \"therefore\". If the only honest connector is \"and then\", the beats have no causal relationship and what you have is a list, not a story. The same facts arranged causally give the viewer a reason to stay; arranged sequentially they give a reason to leave. Every structural choice — engine, act architecture, frame order — inherits this test.",
